# Build context rules for the root image (`docker build .`). Only these paths
# are ever COPY'd by Dockerfile: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE,
# src/ (incl. src/quant_fund/py.typed and
# src/quant_fund/stress/public_domain/fred_h10_h15.json — the wheel
# force-includes) and configs/. Everything below is context-transfer overhead
# (measured 936MB / 22,950 files before this list; see
# .dsh-24x7/lane_reports/l5-packaging.md for the after number).
#
# NOTE (Lead decision 2026-10-08): receipts/, verifier/ and artifacts/ stay IN
# context — docker/research-api.Dockerfile COPYs them (the read-only evidence
# it serves) and a single fail-safe ignore file beats relying on the
# unverified per-Dockerfile ignore-file convention. ~5.4MB total. Image
# content is decided by COPY lines, so the root image still carries none of
# them (root Dockerfile COPYs: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md, LICENSE,
# src/, configs/ only).

# --- VCS / CI / agent state ---
.git
.github
.dsh-24x7
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.serena
.freebuff
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- virtualenvs (2.3GB + 1.2GB) and Python caches ---
# Both bare and ** forms are listed on purpose: plain Go filepath.Match globs
# do not cross "/".
.venv
.venv*
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
**/.hypothesis

# --- coverage / local secrets / local DBs / logs ---
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
mlruns
.mlflow
*.db
**/*.db
*.log
**/*.log

# --- data + heavy trees: never COPY'd (461M / 168M / 97M / 45M / 38M / 31M /
# 25M / 5.6M / 129M) ---
data
rust
web
clients
site
quality
third_party
research
notebooks

# --- build output ---
dist

# --- docs / tests / scripts / work-tracking: not part of the image ---
docs
tests
scripts
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
INFLIGHT
day_grind_progress.md
